WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:07.460
MAHMOUD ELASSIR:
Welcome to the session

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.850
on how Google Cloud's delivering
enterprise transformation

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.080
at scale.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.780
My name is Mahmoud ElAssir.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.000
And I lead customer experience
for our strategic accounts

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.560
at Google Cloud.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.340
I joined Google in late
2019 after spending

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.940
over two decades at Verizon,
where I had multiple technology

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.450
leadership roles, like the
senior vice president and CIO

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.610
for our files business.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.530
And in the past four
and a half years,

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:37.130
I was the senior vice
president and CTO for IT,

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.300
where I led the Verizon
journey to the cloud

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.580
with AWS, Oracle,
GCP, and started

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:47.780
the transformation of Verizon
into a data-driven powerhouse.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:52.940
It's interesting to note how
technology changes so fast.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:56.480
In 2016, AWS was
the right choice

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.050
for datacenter migration,
just like the mainframe

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:02.750
was the right choice
in the '70s and '80s.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:04.940
Today, it's all
about multi-cloud.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.160
It's all about applied AI.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.040
So I cannot be more excited
to be here at Google,

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:15.230
building our enterprise
experience and teams

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:20.780
and helping our most strategic
customers unlock the superior

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.870
capabilities of Google Cloud
and helping them to transform

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:27.010
and win faster.

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.840
Our mission in
customer experience

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:32.770
is to help our customer
adopt and realize value

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:35.230
from Google Cloud solutions.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:38.210
We win when our customers win.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.650
I hope you had a chance to watch
John Jester and Melanie Bragg's

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:45.490
session, which goes
into deep into how

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:49.450
we're investing and building
our customer experience

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:50.890
organization.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.500
Today, I have two objectives.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.460
One, first, I would
like to highlight

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.200
how we're orienting our
customer experience to support

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.970
our most strategic customers.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.690
Then, I want to
share a few examples

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:11.770
on the work we are doing to
support our strategic customers

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.230
across different industries.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:18.650
We're building deep
expertise for enterprise

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.890
in every region
and every industry

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:26.140
to help our customers
transform and win globally.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:28.400
And this list is
growing rapidly,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.350
with many new kind
of partnerships

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:34.500
that we are announcing during
Next OnAir over the nine weeks

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.000
period.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.860
By listening deeply
to our customers,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:48.280
you, we have built our strategy
under Thomas' leadership.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.440
And we are creating a customer
experience organization

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:57.680
with more depth, credibility,
and enterprise readiness.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:01.640
Within customer experience,
we have five main pillars.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.210
Our Professional
Services teams now

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.860
can help you with
datacenter migration,

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:11.420
with mainframe migration,
and with scaling AI and ML

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.350
solutions.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:17.560
We restructured our Support team
to have more customer context

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.230
and to have deeper
expertise in the products

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:22.600
and services of Google Cloud.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:26.380
Also earlier this year, we
launched a premium support

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:29.700
offering with a Mission
Critical Support option

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.730
that will give you
five minutes p0 SLO.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:38.530
Our learning team recently
launched skills and knowledge

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:42.460
badges and certification
program to help

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:47.690
you build deep expertise
into our modern technologies.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:52.400
Our Customer Success Team is
continuously engaging with you

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.180
to help you accelerate the
time to onboard on our cloud

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.100
and to build your
customer success plan,

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:03.090
helping you realize value
faster from our solutions.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.180
And we continuously build
our-- and improve our products

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.540
and services by listening
to you, our customers, also

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:12.040
the feedback we get
from our partners.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:15.980
So that's a huge investment
we're also making this year.

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.130
And lastly, so we're building
my team, which is the--

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.720
I would say the
Transformation Officers Team.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.080
So this is a team of
industry CIOs and CTOs

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.500
that we're hiring to cover
our strategic customers

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.720
in every industry.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.940
And they bring two
items to the table.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:35.040
First, they bring deep
industry knowledge

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.650
in the respective industries
we're focusing on.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.750
And two, they bring
credibility of having

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:46.890
led technology transformation
at scale in that industry.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.260
Let's go a little bit deeper
into these transformation

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.730
officer roles.

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:53.730
There are three key ways
they help you transform.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.940
First of all, they provide
strategic thought leadership

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:00.920
for you and your team through
this transformation journey

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:02.520
and adopting cloud.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.250
And the way, kind of the
transformation officers

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.130
focus on a handful of
clients, up to three customers

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:09.430
at a time.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:11.400
And this will allow them
to spend lots of time

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:15.450
and collaborate with you and
your team to help you be the--

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:19.110
transform your business
and win in your market.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.690
At the same time, these
transformation officers

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:25.140
will act as the coaches
for our Google side

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.820
and continuously
will get our team

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.730
to continuously
de-risk the program

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:33.420
and help them kind of think as
be in the shoes of the customer

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:36.260
and build customer
empathy, continuously

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.620
de-risking to ensure delivery.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:41.400
And the third area, these
transformation officers work

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:45.150
across Google and Google
Cloud with other partners,

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.730
like Google Health and
Verily and Google Travel

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:52.620
and Google Automotive
Services and Android

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.930
and everywhere in Google to
help pool these expertise

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.930
to help you differentiate
in your transformation

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:01.190
and deliver faster.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:04.810
So, as you can see,
you get lots of support

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:06.350
when you work with us.

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:10.610
Here's an example of the
Google Cloud Customer Team.

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.210
As you can see, there
are many individuals

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.450
on this page, all
of whom are here

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:20.530
to support you through this
journey of partnering with us

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:22.680
and migrating to the cloud.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.710
The transformation
officer play key role

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:28.200
in engaging with you and
your leadership team,

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.830
as well as providing
guidance to our account team.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:35.460
This is a service
that we provide

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.882
throughout the delivery.

00:06:36.882 --> 00:06:38.340
And it is something
that we believe

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.031
differentiates Google Cloud.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:44.750
Here are a few examples.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.060
I want to start with the
health care industry.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:50.045
So we just hired Ryan Terry,
who was the business president

00:06:50.045 --> 00:06:53.720
at Hill-Rom, which is a
medical kind of platform,

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.490
device platform.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:59.370
He's done lots of transformation
in the health care industry.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:00.890
So the health care
industry has been

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:04.160
at the forefront of the
fight against COVID,

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:07.340
working tirelessly to
accelerate drug development,

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:10.610
meet heightened demand
for PPE, and rethink

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.650
the delivery of patient care.

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:14.390
There are three areas
we're focusing on

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:17.570
with our health care customers.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:19.370
First one is that telehealth.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.620
The global pandemic has
proven that telehealth

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.350
is an effective way
to deliver care.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:30.080
According to McKinsey research,
consumer adoption of telehealth

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:33.750
has skyrocketed from 11% to 46%.

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:38.270
And 74% of telehealth users
have reported satisfaction.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.460
Our team is working
with several providers

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.790
to build clinical and
patient-friendly telehealth

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:47.510
platforms with easy integration
to hospital scheduling and EHR

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:49.500
systems.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.620
The other area is
advanced clinical research

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.320
with faster times
to drug approval

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:59.020
and better patient
outcomes is a priority.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.470
We are using our
unparalleled tools

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:04.410
in high-performance
computing and AIML

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:08.280
to develop sophisticated models
to expedite the drug discovery

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.440
and approval process.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.780
And finally, we're
working with the hospitals

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:17.220
to enable better decision
making for caregivers

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:20.340
and within business
functions throughout the use

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:24.090
of analytical tools with
more streamlined ways

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:25.995
to access data from
disparate systems.

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:32.440
Shifting gears to the
financial services industry,

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:35.350
and this is where we hired
David Knott as the-- he was

00:08:35.350 --> 00:08:38.650
the chief architect at HSBC.

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:40.799
So our financial
services customers

00:08:40.799 --> 00:08:44.430
are on an exciting journey
and challenging journey also

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:47.100
to redefine the
banking experience.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.380
They all want to transform the
experience for their customers.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.700
They want to reduce risk.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:54.510
And they want to
increase collaboration

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:55.750
among their teams.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:59.100
We're currently partnering
with our financial services

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.870
customers to mainly
do a few things.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.110
One, they want to
migrate off the mainframe

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:07.290
and build cloud native
platforms for banking, which

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:12.720
allow them to innovate more
faster for their customers

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:17.570
and change the experience and
be much more nimble and agile.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:20.390
The other area is they want
to reimagine the customer

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:23.450
experience with the use of
data and machine learning.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.940
And they're building 360
view of the customer, which

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.720
is helping them build more
customized and tailored offers

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:32.610
and services for
their customers.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:36.850
And lastly, we are also
creating new product

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:39.570
with our financial
services customers,

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:44.010
especially when it comes to
fraud and anti-money laundering

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:45.490
and so forth and so on.

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:48.080
And this is where we're
matching their kind of expertise

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:51.750
with our AIML superior
capabilities and talent

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:55.950
to transform and
create these products.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.100
Another industry here
I have is telecom,

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.140
and that's dear to my heart.

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:01.760
We have two
transformation officers

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:04.490
in this space to cover
our customers globally.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:05.520
One is Kevin Shatzkamer.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:09.800
So Kevin recently
joined us from Dell.

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:13.550
He was the CTO for the
service provider industry.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:17.350
And the other one is
Frederic Vanoosthuyze.

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:20.240
And he was the CIO at MegaFon.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.620
So Kevin is on board.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:25.020
Frederic will be
joining us next month.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.290
And we're so excited
to have them.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:31.520
Our telecom customers want to
monetize their 5G investments

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:34.690
and transform into
data-driven powerhouses

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:40.570
to drive both capital
and expense efficiencies.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.340
They're also
looking for new ways

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:46.340
to innovate and provide better
experience for their customers.

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.430
So we're working with
them in three key areas.

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:52.030
The first one is transforming
their customer experience.

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:54.790
So we're launching-- we
launched this product called

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:58.570
Contact Center AI, which
is allowing our telecom

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:01.900
customers to do two things--
transform their customer

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:05.280
experience and their cost
structure at the same time.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.500
Contact Center AI allows
our customers to auto

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:12.190
create both chat
bots and voice bots

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:14.140
with our superior kind
of text-to-speech and

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:17.650
speech-to-text capability,
which is NLP capabilities.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:21.540
And we have amazing
results in this space.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.680
And this product applies
not just to telecom.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:26.950
It applies to any
industry or customer

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.190
that are heavy on call centers.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:35.600
The second area, we're expanding
our mobile Edge footprint

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:39.230
and partnering with multiple
telcos in this space

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:42.470
to transform both the consumer
and create new enterprise

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:46.500
experiences that will harness
the power of low latency

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.280
and high throughput.

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:53.140
Finally, we are using applied
analytics and AIML capabilities

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:57.490
to help our customers drive
efficiency in their capital

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.837
and expense spend
through a tool.

00:11:59.837 --> 00:12:00.670
We have a new tool--

00:12:00.670 --> 00:12:03.050
I encourage everybody to come
and talk to us about it--

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:06.670
called Network Planner.

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:09.350
Shifting gears into travel
and transportation--

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:12.310
so we hired Ravi
Simhambhatla from-- he

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:14.170
was the CTO at United Airlines.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.830
Ravi has been on board for the
past-- since earlier this year.

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:20.530
And he's been heavily engaged
with our strategic customers

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:23.110
in the travel business.

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:24.540
And there are few
industries that

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:27.710
have been more impacted by
COVID than the travel industry.

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:31.240
And rather than scaling
back their investments,

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:33.880
we have seen our customers
use this opportunity

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:36.580
to accelerate their
digital transformation.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:39.340
And we are very proud
to be supporting them

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.290
during these times.

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:44.350
Some of the key areas we're
working with our customers

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:46.480
across this industry are--

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:49.510
so one is getting them
of their data centers

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:51.130
and getting them
off the mainframe

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:54.670
into our cloud platform and
helping them change the culture

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:58.250
to be much more agile,
build DevOps, and build

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.560
SRE for operations.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:04.510
The other area is they're using
our superior AIML capabilities

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:08.320
and talent to drive efficiencies
in their operations,

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.657
and especially their
irregular operations.

00:13:10.657 --> 00:13:12.490
Basically, when the
weather, there's a storm

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:14.620
and they need to
reschedule everything, so

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:16.180
how do you use AIML for that?

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:20.320
How do you plan the
last-mile routing?

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.960
So lots of opportunities here
to reinvent that business

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:26.430
with our superior capabilities.

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.560
And finally, we're also
partnering with them.

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:31.530
And there's an area where we
call Google Travel into this,

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:35.360
and to help create new products
and services for both consumer

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.270
and enterprise customers,
and allow them to make

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:40.520
new kind of types of revenue.

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:42.170
So these are a few
examples I share

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:45.350
with you of the work we're
doing across supporting

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:48.440
to support our customers
transform and differentiate

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:50.950
and innovate across
multiple industries.

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:52.260
There are many more examples.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:57.540
I'm happy to talk about them
more in a different occasion.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:14:02.320
In closing, I'd like to leave
you with three key takeaways.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:06.910
The first one, I hope you
see the customer centricity.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:11.010
We at Google Cloud are all
about you, our customers,

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:14.790
and helping you realize
value through our products

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.050
and solutions.

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:21.510
The second one-- we continue to
make big investments to support

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:23.700
you, our enterprise customers.

